  "body": "What happens:\nIn the operation property panel, when the user selects a face or edge in the viewport as the geometry source for a toolpath operation, the \"source\" dropdown reverts to \"stock\". The user expects it to show \"selection\" or at least stay on \"model\". This confuses the user because they cannot tell whether their face/edge pick was actually applied.\n\nExpected:\nThe source dropdown shows \"selection\" when the user has picked faces or edges, or at least stays on \"model\" so the user knows their pick is active.\n\nEvidence:\nFound while using Rotary Parallel with face selection on the first-continuous-4axis-part example. After picking faces in the viewport, the source dropdown shows \"stock\" even though the operation is using the selected faces.\n\nDone means:\n- The source dropdown reflects the actual geometry source: \"selection\" when faces/edges are picked, \"model\" when the whole model is used, \"stock\" when stock is the source\n- The dropdown does not revert to \"stock\" after a valid face/edge pick\n- The user can tell at a glance whether their pick is active",
